; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Guilloche Rosette
; CATEGORY: Patterns & Mandalas
; LEVEL:    Advanced
; TAGS:     guilloche, polar coordinates, sine waves, phase, banknote art
; SUMMARY:  Draws the fine woven line rosettes found on banknotes and certificates, from wavy circles shifted a little at a time.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Look closely at a banknote and you will see delicate rosettes of
;   thin overlapping lines. They are called guilloche patterns and
;   were first cut by machines with spinning gears. Here each line is
;   a circle whose radius wobbles up and down like a sine wave. Many
;   copies, each with its wobble shifted a little, weave a band. Three
;   bands of different sizes and wobbles make the rosette.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Each line in the BANDS list describes one band:
;   radius, wobble size, wobbles per turn, a second smaller wobble,
;   number of lines, and color. Change them and run again.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * polar coordinates: a point from an angle and a distance
;   * a sine wave wrapped round a circle
;   * phase: the same wave started a bit later
;   * adding two waves together for a more complex shape
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Make the number of lines equal to the wobbles per turn.
;   * Set the second wobble to 0 for a simpler, cleaner band.
;   * Use a thicker pen and fewer lines for a bold poster look.
; ============================================================

; [radius wobble waves wobble2 waves2 lines color]
make "bands [
  [235 22 24 6 8 14 [30 90 120]]
  [150 34 12 10 4 16 [150 40 90]]
  [62 30 6 6 18 18 [200 120 20]]
]

; One wavy circle. The distance from the center at angle a is
; radius + wobble x sin(waves x a + phase) + wobble2 x sin(waves2 x a - phase).
to wavycircle :r :w1 :k1 :w2 :k2 :phase
  for [a 0 360 2] [
    localmake "d :r + :w1 * (sin :k1 * :a + :phase) + :w2 * (sin :k2 * :a - :phase)
    ifelse :a = 0 [penup] [pendown]
    setxy :d * sin :a :d * cos :a
  ]
  penup
end

; A band: :lines copies, each with its wave shifted by an equal
; share of one full wave (360 degrees of phase).
to band :spec
  localmake "lines item 6 :spec
  setpencolor item 7 :spec
  for [i 0 :lines - 1] [
    wavycircle item 1 :spec item 2 :spec item 3 :spec item 4 :spec item 5 :spec 360 * :i / :lines
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [248 244 232]
setpensize 1
foreach :bands [band ?]
; a fine double ring at the edge, like on a certificate
setpencolor [30 90 120]
penup home pendown
arc 360 282
arc 360 287
